  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Quinisocaine (dimethisoquin) is a local anesthetic applied to the skin, used topically to relieve itching. It is not an established marketed medicine today; databases list it only as an experimental compound, with no EU authorisation.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1478199&quot;>Wikidata Q1478199</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>quinisocaine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>D04AB05</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13683&quot;>DB13683</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/6857&quot;>6857</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:93295&quot;>93295</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1478199&quot;>Q1478199</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C17H24N2O</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>272.392 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
